== SIBLING PARITY ==
  The five decline sites vs the LEGAL direction of the same case.  Declines (X6): {seeded, all-zero} x latch {clear =
    first, set = repeat}.  Legal accesses: latch SET only, both states (X7); latch CLEAR only in the SEEDED state (X2 len
    1/2 reads, X8 len 4 reads at wide seeds, X5 the zero Clear write).  ASYMMETRY: LEGAL x ALL-ZERO x LATCH-CLEAR has no
    row, and it is the reset state -- jointly reachable through the device's own data flow (DEVINIT's memset).
    OWED: X9, every legal access with the latches CLEAR, in every state.
  Seed width: every X6/X7 seed fits in ONE byte (0x18/0x30/0x60/0xc0); X8 widened the LEGAL READ values only, so a
    decline or a latch clearer keyed on bits 8-31 of a field passes every row (Fable Q2's (e) cell).  OWED: a WIDE
    state (0x80010018 / 0x00010030 / 0x40020060 / 0x000200c0, X8's seeds) as a third state of X6, X7 and X9.

== CLAIM -> ROW ==
  diff_footbridge.c X6/X7 CONTRACT: "the cells above are the whole class for these five sites" -- MEASURED FALSE (Q1..Q5).
    Rewritten: the class is ACCESS {declined, legal} x STATE {seeded, all-zero, wide} x LATCH {clear, set}; X9 carries
    LEGAL x LATCH-CLEAR; the DEPENDS-ON bound is stated as BOTH branches under the direction test (Fable Q1, D1).
  new X9 header "a legal access from latch-clear announces nothing, returns its value and consumes no latch" -> every X9
    row: announce 0 during the access, and the five declines that follow announce EXACTLY 5.
  new X9 header "the enable writes behave as written" -> X9 write rows: the enable field as expected, the other three
    unchanged, IRQ Set/Clear exactly one assert or one deassert by (irq_status & new enable), FIQ Set/Clear none.

== GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD ==
  Dominating predicates at each edited decline, up to the function boundary: the case label; the DIRECTION test
    (`writeflag == MEM_READ` at IRQ_STATUS, IRQ_RAW_STATUS, FIQ_STATUS, FIQ_RAW_STATUS; `writeflag == MEM_WRITE` at
    IRQ_ENABLE_CLEAR); the latch `!d->warned_*`.
  Body-read lvalues, BOTH branches under the direction test: the read branches read irq_status/irq_enable/fiq_status/
    fiq_enable; the Clear write branch reads and writes irq_enable, reads irq_status, calls ASSERT/DEASSERT; the
    decline branches read and write only their own latch.
  The (d) forms this adds: `&& F` and `&& !F` on the direction test, F in {irq_status, irq_enable, fiq_status,
    fiq_enable}.  `&& F` diverts a legal access when F == 0 (all-zero -> X9 all-zero); `&& !F` diverts when F != 0
    (seeded, wide -> X9 seeded/wide).  Q1..Q5 are the `&& F` members the adjudication named.
  Disagreeing state owed: all-zero with the latches clear, and a state with bits above byte 0 (wide).

